<title>USA: Johnson &amp; Johnson unit files for cancer drug.</title>
<headline>Johnson &amp; Johnson unit files for cancer drug.</headline>
<dateline>TITUSVILLE, N.J. 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Janssen Research Foundation, a unit of Johnson &amp; Johnson, said Tuesday it has filed a new drug application with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for its Liazal, a prostate cancer drug.</p>
<p>The foundation said it is seeking approval to use Liazal to manage metastatic prostate cancer, which is cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, after hormonal therapies have failed.</p>
